<div class="hd"><div class="wrap"><h1>About Leadedge Academy</h1><p class="lead">A corporate learning and development partner focused on practical, measurable results.</p></div></div>
<div class="sec"><div class="wrap two top rv"><div><i class="tick"></i><h2>Who we are</h2><p>Leadedge Academy is a corporate training and professional development practice based in Hyderabad, founded by Raghu Jupudi, an L&amp;D professional with 15 years of experience. We work with retail and corporate organisations to build employee capability, strengthen leadership and improve performance.</p><p>We are a focused, founder-led practice. That means the person who understands your requirement is the person who designs and delivers your programme.</p><h3 style="margin-top:34px">Our purpose</h3><p>To make professional learning practical, accessible and impactful, so that people grow and organisations see the difference.</p></div>
<div><i class="tick"></i><h2>Our training philosophy</h2><p>Adults learn by doing. We therefore keep input short and practice long: real scenarios, case studies, role plays and assignments drawn from your own environment.</p><p>Training only matters if behaviour changes. We design for application on the job, and we plan how learning will be reinforced and evaluated after the session ends.</p><p>People are the greatest strength of any organisation. Investing in their growth is investing in the future.</p></div></div></div>
<div class="sec dk"><div class="wrap rv"><i class="tick"></i><h2>How capability connects to business performance</h2><p class="lead">Our organisational development approach follows a simple chain. Each link is addressed deliberately in our programmes.</p>
<div class="chain"><div><b>Capability</b><span>Skills, knowledge and mindset are built.</span></div><div><b>Behaviour</b><span>New practices are applied on the job.</span></div><div><b>Performance</b><span>Teams work more consistently and confidently.</span></div><div><b>Business outcomes</b><span>Service, sales and productivity improve.</span></div></div></div></div>
<div class="sec"><div class="wrap two top rv"><div><i class="tick"></i><h2>Why practical learning matters</h2><p>Theory alone rarely survives a busy week. Practical learning gives people the chance to rehearse real conversations, make decisions on real cases and take back tools they can use the next morning.</p><p>For managers it means better coaching and planning. For frontline teams it means confident customer conversations. For the organisation it means learning spend tied to business needs.</p></div>
<div><i class="tick"></i><h2>How we work</h2><ul class="list"><li>Corporate training at client premises</li><li>Online training programmes</li><li>Virtual workshops</li><li>Corporate consulting on learning needs</li><li>Customised training programmes</li></ul></div></div></div>
</section>

